# Requests against the local stack (docker compose up --build --wait).
# Run them top to bottom. Works with the REST Client extension for VS Code and with the
# HTTP client built into Visual Studio; the expected answer is noted above each request.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@cart = {{host}}/api/v1/cart

### Ready? 200 Healthy
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### A development token for the user "alice". Run this before the cart requests. 200
# @name token
POST {{host}}/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "alice"}

### The token is taken from the answer above. In a tool that does not support that, replace
### the value below with the accessToken you copied.
@accessToken = {{token.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The empty cart. 200
GET {{cart}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Put two T-shirts in the cart. 200, one line
PUT {{cart}}/items/TSHIRT-BLK-M
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 2}

### Add a mug. 200, two lines
PUT {{cart}}/items/MUG-WHT
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 1}

### Set the T-shirts to three. The quantity replaces the old one; it is never added. 200
PUT {{cart}}/items/TSHIRT-BLK-M
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 3}

### The cart with both lines. 200
GET {{cart}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Remove the mug. 200, one line
DELETE {{cart}}/items/MUG-WHT
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Remove everything. 200, no lines; the cart keeps its id
DELETE {{cart}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### A quantity outside 1 to 99. 400 validation_failed
PUT {{cart}}/items/MUG-WHT
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 0}

### A product that does not exist. 404 product_not_found
PUT {{cart}}/items/NO-SUCH-PRODUCT
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 1}

### No token. 401
GET {{cart}}
